      "title": "South Korea pushes back on reports it is readying Hormuz deployment amid US pressure",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/04/south-korea-pushes-back-reports-hormuz-deployment-us-pressure",
      "description": "<p>Seoul reportedly seeking parliamentary approval to send military assets to Middle East but president’s office plays down claims</p><p>South Korea is reviewing a possible deployment of military assets to the strait of Hormuz amid pressure from Donald Trump over Seoul’s reluctance to provide support in the region, according to domestic media reports.</p><p>Citing unnamed government and military sources, the reports published on Thursday and Friday said preparations were under way and that the government intended to seek parliamentary approval for a new deployment. The reports, which appeared in major South Korean outlets, said the exact scale and timing had not been agreed.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/04/south-korea-pushes-back-reports-hormuz-deployment-us-pressure\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-04T07:47:41"
    },
